# Git: Push after every change

After making any code or script changes in this repository:

1. Commit with a concise message (focus on why), **authored only as nycon** (see `commits-as-nycon.mdc` — no Cursor co-author).
2. Push to `origin/main` immediately — do not wait for the user to ask.
3. Only skip push if the user explicitly said not to commit/push in that turn.

Do not leave completed work only on the local machine.
